## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of docker-dca basics, per-tenant gating, and config management in real deployments across DCs.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for feature flags
- Hot reload of config without restart
- Tenant-scoped feature gating via header X-Tenant-ID
- TLS termination with Nginx and cross-DC routing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal per-tenant feature gating middleware
const fs = require('fs');
let features = {};
function load(){
  try{ features = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/config/flags.json','utf8')); }catch(e){ features = {}; }
}
load();
setInterval(load, 30000);
module.exports = function(req,res,next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  if (tenant && features[tenant] && features[tenant].includes('payments')) return next();
  res.status(403).send('Feature disabled');
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate config schema and handle partial reloads?
- How would you extend to multiple features and tenants with minimal latency impact?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design dynamic, per-tenant tracing in a multi-DC docker-dca setup, including config retrieval, TTL-based caching, and graceful degradation when the sidecar cannot fetch config.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry sampling and per-tenant configuration
- Consul KV as a central per-tenant policy store
- TTL caching to limit external calls
- Graceful fallback to sensible default rate
- Cross-DC deployment considerations and observability impact

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-sampler for per-tenant tracing
class TenantSampler {
  constructor(fetchRate) {
    this.fetchRate = fetchRate; // function(tenant) -> rate
    this.cache = new Map(); // tenant -> {rate, expiry}
  }
  getRate(tenant) {
    const entry = this.cache.get(tenant);
    if (entry && entry.expiry > Date.now()) return entry.rate;
    // fetch from Consul KV here, then cache for 5s
    const rate = this.fetchRate(tenant) ?? 20;
    this.cache.set(tenant, { rate, expiry: Date.now() + 5000 });
    return rate;
  }
  shouldSample(tenant) {
    const rate = this.getRate(tenant);
    return Math.random() * 100 < rate;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test correctness of per-tenant rates during rollout?
- What are failure modes if Consul KV is unavailable, and how to mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical ability to extend a docker-dca setup with a compliant, low-latency data-redaction path.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config-driven per-tenant policies
- Sidecar pattern and in-memory caching
- Streaming JSON redaction without full buffering
- Nginx-edge integration and TLS context

## Code Example
```go
package main
import (
  "encoding/json"
  "fmt"
)
func redact(m map[string]interface{}, fields map[string]bool){
  for k,v := range m {
    if fields[k] { m[k] = "***REDACTED***"; continue }
    if mm, ok := v.(map[string]interface{}); ok { redact(mm, fields) }
    if arr, ok := v.([]interface{}); ok {
      for _, it := range arr { if sub, ok := it.(map[string]interface{}); ok { redact(sub, fields) } }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test nested JSON redaction with large bodies?
- How would you monitor redaction performance without affecting latency?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical skills in cross-DC coordination, configuration management, and state synchronization using Docker Config and Redis Pub/Sub. It also covers rate limiting and error handling under load.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for storing per-tenant quota limits
- Redis PUB/SUB for cross-DC quota propagation
- Quota checks with eventual consistency across peers
- TLS edge routing with Traefik

## Code Example
```javascript
const quota = getQuota(tenantId);
if (quota <= 0) throw new Error('Quota exceeded');

await performImport(data);
decrementQuota(tenantId);
publishQuotaUpdate(tenantId, getQuota(tenantId));
```

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical secret lifecycle management in Docker Swarm, integrating Vault for automated rotation with zero-downtime upgrades and proper secret versioning.

## Key Concepts
- Swarm secrets versioning and dynamic reattachment
- Vault-based rotation triggers and secret provisioning
- Rolling updates with start-first strategy to avoid downtime
- Health checks to confirm new secrets are loaded before removing old ones
- Atomic secret updates using add-then-remove pattern

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-automation: rotate Vault-derived Swarm secrets
async function rotateSecrets(serviceName, vaultPath) {
  // Fetch new credentials from Vault
  const newCreds = await vault.read(vaultPath);

  // Create new Swarm secrets
  const newSecrets = await createSwarmSecrets(newCreds);

  // Update service with new secrets
  await updateService(serviceName, newSecrets);

  // Verify health before cleanup
  await verifyServiceHealth(serviceName);

  // Remove old secrets
  await cleanupOldSecrets(serviceName);
}
```
